  {"id":"atompunk","name":"Atompunk","cat":"net","era":"imagined 1950s futures","y":1950,"essence":"Nuclear-glow optimism: chrome fins, ray guns and a trust in technology that World War II had not yet broken.","origin":"A retrofuturist label for the hopeful 1950s idea of an atomic-powered future (flying cars, nuclear homes), named online well after the fact alongside steampunk and dieselpunk.","fuzzy":"Overlaps heavily with Raygun Gothic and Space Age design; the three names are mostly a matter of which decade's optimism is being pictured.","light":"Bright googie-sign neon, clean laboratory white","materials":["chrome","formica","atomic-pattern textile","glass"],"motifs":["atom diagrams","starbursts","ray guns","flying saucers"],"mood":["optimistic","futuristic","retro","bright"],"related":["raygun-gothic","space-age","dieselpunk","cassette-futurism"],"aw":"Atompunk","pals":[{"n":"Nuclear optimism","c":[["#2E7FB2","Nice Blue",0.22,2.4],["#F2C230","Sunglow",0.2,2.6],["#D9412E","Dusty vermilion",0.16,2.3],["#C9C2A8","Olive-Buff",0.22,3],["#1C1C1A","Eerie Black",0.2,1.5]]},{"n":"Measured overall","c":[["#231B1B","Raisin Black",0.315,3.9],["#E3B84E","Primuline Yellow",0.152,3.2],["#3D2E2D","Reddish Black",0.146,2.7],["#AF6034","Earth",0.142,3.8],["#816D4D","Grey Brown",0.126,2.4],["#492D19","Café Noir",0.12,4.4]]},{"n":"Measured darks","c":[["#231B1B","Raisin Black",0.386,3.9],["#3D2E2D","Reddish Black",0.179,2.7],["#492D19","Café Noir",0.147,4.4],["#7E4D31","Auburn",0.145,2.7],["#322C26","Dark walnut",0.144,4.3]]},{"n":"Measured lights","c":[["#E3B84E","Primuline Yellow",0.338,3.2],["#C1CFDB","Pale Aqua",0.202,2.8],["#E69A21","Marigold",0.181,2.6],["#D29C76","Light cinnamon",0.148,2.2],["#E3C49E","Pale flesh",0.131,1.9]]},{"n":"Measured accents","c":[["#E3B84E","Primuline Yellow",0.249,3.2],["#AF6034","Earth",0.233,3.8],["#974833","Chestnut",0.186,1.9],["#C23E21","Brazil Red",0.175,3.7],["#3B4890","Cyanine Blue",0.156,2.8]]}]},
  {"id":"cluttercore","name":"Cluttercore","cat":"net","era":"2020s","y":2021,"essence":"Every shelf full, every wall covered: a deliberate, colorful rebellion against minimalism.","origin":"Spread on TikTok and Instagram in the early 2020s as a reaction against the pared-back minimalist interiors that had dominated home-design feeds for years.","fuzzy":"Defined mostly by what it refuses (empty surfaces, neutral palettes); any sufficiently full, colorful room can be called cluttercore.","light":"Warm layered lamp light, daylight through packed shelves","materials":["mismatched ceramics","vintage textiles","houseplants","framed art stacks"],"motifs":["packed bookshelves","gallery walls","collected trinkets","layered textiles"],"mood":["maximal","personal","joyful","lived-in"],"related":["memphis","postmodern","chaotic-academia"],"aw":"Cluttercore","pals":[{"n":"Full shelf","c":[["#C9472E","Dusty vermilion",0.18,3],["#2E8F7A","Illuminating Emerald",0.18,1.8],["#E8B83B","Primuline Yellow",0.16,2],["#6E4A9A","Campanula",0.16,2.7],["#2E2B28","Dark gunmetal",0.16,2.7],["#D9CBAE","Pale Olive-Buff",0.16,1.6]]},{"n":"Measured overall","c":[["#140F0F","Smoky Black",0.347,2.3],["#393129","Blackish Brown",0.176,3.5],["#BDB9B4","Warm silver",0.151,3.3],["#504E46","Umbra Grey",0.11,2.4],["#7F766E","Benzo Brown",0.11,3.8],["#3A1915","Dark Sienna",0.106,2.8]]},{"n":"Measured darks","c":[["#140F0F","Smoky Black",0.413,2.3],["#393129","Blackish Brown",0.209,3.5],["#504E46","Umbra Grey",0.131,2.4],["#3A1915","Dark Sienna",0.127,2.8],["#6E2D1E","Mahogany",0.12,0.6]]},{"n":"Measured accents","c":[["#6E2D1E","Mahogany",0.375,0.6],["#975836","Sienna",0.26,3.2],["#AF6943","Brown Sugar",0.161,2.1],["#CB4618","Sinopia",0.126,1.4],["#6C934B","Moss green",0.078,1.7]]}]}
